<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Borovsk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Borovsk is a small town in Kaluga Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, on the Protva river south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. In the 14th century it belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serpukhov">Serpukhov</a>. It is known for the Pafnutiev Borovsky Monastery, founded in 1444, and as the place where the Old Believer noblewoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feodosia">Feodosia</a> Morozova was imprisoned and died in 1675.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/borovsk.jpg" alt="Borovsk" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Участник:Nesusvet. Original uploader was Nesusvet at ru.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Borovsk.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
